  "description": {
   "value": "<p><strong>Cost:</strong> 250eb (Expensive) <strong>♦</strong> <strong>Required Slots:</strong> 1</p>\n<p><strong>Fits:</strong> All Crossbows</p>\n<p><em>Since ancient times, humans have used levers, pulleys, winches, or cranks to make use of almost excessively heavy draw weights.</em></p>\n<p>As an Action, the weapon’s user may cock the Cocking Lever to pull back the drawstring with greater tensile energy. After using the Cocking Lever, the weapon’s next Attack deals 1d6 additional damage, and whenever it would ablate armor, ablates 1 additional SP. The Cocking Device then provides no bonuses until it is cocked again. This increase in damage is counted as applying to the weapon’s standard Single Shot damage for the purposes of the Upsized Power Mod.</p>\n<p><strong>Attachment slots:</strong> 1</p>\n<p><em>From <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13EnSAoiLDsC7zmL-Jr1RqIh_EnuVuFnExqiipDVquMk/edit\">Corgo's 77 Collection V3</a> by Corgopolis (Weapons &gt; Attachment Catalog &gt; Grips &amp; Controls).</em></p>"
